# Who has to look at a change before it reaches `main`.
#
# `main` is what the world downloads. Everything in the repository is owned by the maintainer, so a
# pull request into `main` needs their review — which is the gate, stated as a rule rather than
# left as a convention people are expected to remember.
#
# This says nothing about `next`. Work lands there on its own steam: a collaborator opens a pull
# request, the checks run, and they merge it themselves. The gate is promotion, not contribution.

